sections.content:
With the next statement, we can skip an iteration without terminating the loop:

Example
Skip "banana":

 fruits <- list("apple", "banana", "cherry")

for (x in fruits) {

 if (x == "banana") {
    next
  }
  print(x)

 }

Try it Yourself »

When the loop passes "banana", it will skip it and continue to loop.

