sections.content:
It is also possible to place a loop inside another loop. This is called a nested loop:

Example
Print the adjective of each fruit in a list:

 adj <- list("red", "big", "tasty")

fruits <- list("apple", "banana", 
 "cherry")
  for (x in adj) {
    for (y in fruits) {

 print(paste(x, y))
  }
}

Try it Yourself »

